{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells, revealing simultaneous nucleation at dual interfaces during processing. By designing a self-segregating molecule (NFA), the researchers synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and create hydrophobic barriers. The approach achieves record power conversion efficiencies (24.84% for small cells, 21.46% for modules) with stable performance after 1000 hours of damp aging.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Self-segregating NFA molecule synchronizes dual-interface crystallization and passivates defects",
    "Devices maintain 96.26% efficiency after 1000 hours of damp aging at 85±5% RH"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a general strategy to resolve kinetic-environmental trade-offs in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells, advancing stability and efficiency in scalable photovoltaic systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This review reassesses the pro-tumor role of M2-like tumor-associated macrophages (TAMs) by evaluating functional evidence from tumor-derived cells. It examines phagocytosis, antigen processing, cross-presentation, and CD8+ T cell activation. Key findings indicate that some CD206+ TAMs can cross-present tumor antigens and activate CD8+ T cells comparably to dendritic cells, correlating with improved outcomes. Conversely, other macrophages may promote immunosuppression. The study emphasizes that antigen fate and co-stimulatory context, not M1/M2 markers, determine functional outcomes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CD206+ tumor-associated macrophages can cross-present tumor antigens and activate CD8+ T cells at levels matching conventional dendritic cells",
    "These functional capabilities correlate with better clinical outcomes in specific contexts",
    "Antigen-presenting macrophages may either activate cytotoxic T cells or promote regulatory T cell activity depending on co-stimulatory signals"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes that functional assays, not surface markers alone, define the immunological role of tumor-associated macrophages in cancer, shifting the paradigm from marker-based classification to context-dependent mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates why early humans settled only briefly in 'Green Arabia' despite abundant freshwater. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across the Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable stone at 55 of 125 surveyed sites with palaeolake deposits. The results indicate that early human settlement required both water and accessible stone for tool production, not water alone, challenging previous models of human dispersal into arid regions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable stone were found at 55 of 125 sites with palaeolake deposits",
    "Settlement patterns tracked co-occurrence of water and lithic raw materials rather than water alone",
    "57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, improving site discrimination accuracy to 0.768"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic raw material availability is a critical, previously overlooked constraint in early human dispersal models across arid landscapes, refining predictions of habitable ranges for stone-tool-dependent populations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and its role in gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors, leading to ILC3 depletion and increased susceptibility to enteric infections. The study demonstrated that PRKAR1A maintains ILC3 homeostasis in adults by restraining PKA activity, and IL-23 overproduction triggers inflammation via PKA dysregulation in human gut ILC3s.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Prostaglandin activates PKA to upregulate tissue-protective factors in ILC3s",
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (e.g., PRKAR1A), reducing ILC3s and increasing infection susceptibility",
    "PRKAR1A maintains ILC3 homeostasis in adults by restraining PKA activity, with IL-23 overproduction causing gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3-mediated gut homeostasis and identifies IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation as a mechanism for intestinal inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how maternal and early life obesity impacts adaptive immune responses during childhood vaccination. Using a mouse model replicating the obesity-epidemiological link, researchers found that high-fat diet exposure in pregnancy or early life, but not adulthood, altered naive CD4+ T cell epigenetics and transcriptional profiles. This impaired T follicular helper cell differentiation and germinal center reactions to mRNA and protein vaccines. Mechanistically, epigenetic repression of A20 (Tnfaip3) drove these defects, with pediatric A20 haploinsufficiency correlating with reduced TFH cells. The findings establish maternal and early life obesity as critical determinants of vaccine immunity during development.",
  "key_findings": [
    "High-fat diet exposure during pregnancy or early life, but not adulthood, reshaped naive CD4+ T cell epigenetics and transcriptional profiles",
    "Epigenetic repression of A20 (Tnfaip3) impaired T follicular helper cell differentiation and germinal center reactions to vaccines",
    "Pediatric A20 haploinsufficiency correlated with reduced circulating T follicular helper cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies maternal and early life obesity as key determinants of adaptive immune responses during critical developmental windows, providing mechanistic insights into how obesity programs CD4+ T cell fate to impair vaccine efficacy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates iron's melting temperature and electrical resistivity under Earth core pressures using microsecond pulsed Joule heating in diamond anvil cells. Over 300 reproducible melting measurements reveal a shallow melting curve, reaching 6 K/GPa and 4160 ± 80 K at 200 GPa. The findings suggest a relatively cold core-mantle boundary (3430 K) and low adiabatic outer core heat flow (9.8 TW), indicating thermal convection could have powered the geodynamo before inner core formation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A shallow melting curve for iron at 200 GPa, reaching 6 K/GPa and 4160 ± 80 K",
    "Inferred core-mantle boundary temperature of 3430 K",
    "Low adiabatic outer core heat flow of 9.8 TW"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides critical constraints on Earth's core thermal evolution, revealing that thermal convection alone may have driven the geodynamo prior to inner core formation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility between cocatalysts in alkaline and pure water systems as a critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and surface kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of cocatalyst incompatibility between alkaline and pure water splitting systems as a bottleneck for stable Ta3N5 photocatalysis",
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieved 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting over nitride materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing efficient solar-driven water splitting systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated regulatory T-cell dynamics in cirrhotic HCV genotype 4 patients during and after direct-acting antiviral therapy. Using longitudinal blood sampling and flow cytometry, researchers assessed T-cell subsets at baseline, treatment, and 1 year post-viral clearance. Results showed baseline immune dysregulation with reduced T cells, exhausted CD8+ T cells, and expanded Tregs. By 1 year post-SVR, Tregs normalized, exhausted CD8+ cells decreased significantly, and TH17 cells declined, indicating partial immune recovery after viral clearance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Baseline cirrhotic patients exhibited reduced CD3+ T cells and profound CD8+ T-cell exhaustion (PD-1+ 71.0% vs. 11.1%)",
    "Tregs expanded at baseline (52.7% vs. 15.1% in controls) and normalized to 9.6% by 1 year post-SVR",
    "Exhausted PD-1+ CD8+ cells declined by 66.2% and CD38+ CD8+ cells decreased by 31.3% within 1 year of treatment"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study demonstrates that successful HCV antiviral therapy in cirrhotic patients partially corrects T-cell immune dysregulation, providing insights into the immunological recovery process post-viral clearance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window prevents amplification. Mechanistically, HFD recruits neutrophils expressing NLRP3 and IL-1β, which license pathogenic TH17 cells. Post-recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. These findings demonstrate that short-lived dietary states during specific temporal windows can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates skin inflammation to chronic obesity levels",
    "Switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the same window prevents inflammatory amplification",
    "Neutrophil-mediated NLRP3-IL-1β signaling licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, leading to persistent tissue-resident memory T cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study reveals that transient dietary states during acute inflammation can durably reprogram immune memory, highlighting a critical temporal window for dietary interventions to influence long-term inflammatory responses."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines public criticism regarding the Pathogen Hunters group's extensive global sampling and its genetic data interpretation. The research addresses concerns about the scale and complexity of their infectious disease surveillance efforts, highlighting potential methodological challenges in large-scale pathogen genomics without specifying exact findings.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Public scrutiny of Pathogen Hunters' global sampling scale",
    "Criticism of genetic data interpretation complexity",
    "Methodological challenges in large-scale pathogen genomics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings underscore the importance of transparent methodology in global pathogen surveillance initiatives, emphasizing the need for rigorous validation of large-scale genomic data to ensure reliable infectious disease monitoring."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how 4f electron filling influences bonding evolution in lanthanide single-atom catalysts across the series. Using structurally uniform catalysts, researchers identified a dual-periodic trend in lanthanide-support and adsorbate binding energies, increasing from La to Eu and Gd to Yb. The half-filled 4f7 configuration at Eu-Gd transition drives abrupt changes, while consistent crystal-field splitting enables robust linear relationships across coordination environments. These findings establish a 4f-electron-regulated framework for lanthanide reactivity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dual-periodic trend in lanthanide-support binding energies increases from La to Eu and Gd to Yb",
    "The half-filled 4f7 configuration at Eu-Gd transition induces abrupt changes in bonding energies",
    "Consistent crystal-field splitting enables robust linear relationships between binding and bonding energies across diverse coordination environments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a fundamental 4f-electron-regulated bonding framework for understanding lanthanide reactivity, providing intrinsic electronic principles for catalyst design beyond system-specific phenomena."
}

{
  "summary": "This case report investigates corticosteroid-refractory autoimmune hepatitis type 1 (AIH-1) using a standardized Boswellia serrata extract. A 47-year-old patient with AIH-1 relapsed during prednisolone tapering and was intolerant to azathioprine and mycophenolate mofetil. Adjunctive Boswellia extract (300 mg three times daily) during a corticosteroid taper normalized alanine aminotransferase, reduced immunoglobulin G, and decreased prednisolone dose. Flow cytometry showed increased Treg/Th17 ratio from 0.4 to 1.2. Biochemical remission was maintained at 18 months without adverse events. The findings suggest potential adjunctive steroid-sparing efficacy for selected refractory AIH-1 cases.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Normalization of alanine aminotransferase within 12 weeks of Boswellia extract adjunctive therapy",
    "Reduction in immunoglobulin G from 22.4 to 12.1 g/L",
    "Increased Treg/Th17 ratio from 0.4 to 1.2 with sustained biochemical remission at 18 months"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This case report provides hypothesis-generating evidence for Boswellia serrata extract as a potential adjunctive therapy in corticosteroid-refractory autoimmune hepatitis type 1, suggesting immunomodulatory mechanisms that warrant prospective validation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used genome-wide data from 4,587 ancient individuals across Bronze and Iron Age Europe to investigate Celtic language dispersal. It identified three key demographic processes: Steppe-related ancestry arrival via Bell Beaker groups (~4400 BP), Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain, and westward expansion of Knovíz-Urnfield-related ancestry (3200-2800 BP) affecting France, the British Isles, and Italy. The findings suggest eastern central European origins as the most parsimonious model for Celtic spread, though language shifts may not directly track genetic changes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry entered Europe via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Knovíz-Urnfield-related ancestry expanded westward from eastern central Europe (3200-2800 BP) influencing France, the British Isles, and Italy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides genomic evidence supporting eastern central European origins as the most plausible demographic pathway for Celtic language dispersal in prehistoric Europe."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether climate aridity independently drives nitrate pollution beyond human inputs using machine-learning reconstructed global river maps. It found climate aridity systematically elevates nitrate concentrations across land-use gradients, creating hotspots outside major agricultural and urban areas. Nitrate concentrations exceed ecological thresholds across 33% of global land area and health thresholds in 2% of land area, affecting billions of people. The findings indicate nitrate pollution is amplified by aridity, suggesting aridification could increase exposure without additional human inputs.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Climate aridity elevates nitrate concentrations across land-use gradients, creating hotspots outside major agricultural and urban centers",
    "Nitrate concentrations exceed ecological thresholds across 33% of global land area and health thresholds in 2% of land area",
    "Aridification may increase nitrate exposure without additional human inputs"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that climate aridity is a dominant driver of nitrate pollution, challenging the assumption that human inputs alone cause nitrate pollution and highlighting the need for climate-informed regulatory approaches."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how organizing identical hydrogen-bonded aramide motifs into progressively complex architectures—foldamer, macrocycle, and cage—affects iodine capture performance. By comparing these structures, the research demonstrates stepwise improvements in uptake capacity, kinetics, and retention, with each motif contributing more than additively. The cage architecture achieves the highest reported iodine capture efficiency, capturing up to 84 I3- per molecule despite high anion competition.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Progressive architectural organization of aramide motifs enhances iodine capture capacity stepwise from foldamers to cages",
    "Each motif contributes non-additively to iod: capture, with cage structures achieving up to 84 I3- per molecule",
    "Cage architectures maintain high iodine capture efficiency in competitive anion environments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a design principle for amplifying adsorption performance through hierarchical organization of molecular motifs, advancing understanding of how structural complexity can enhance functional properties in adsorbent materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether emotional stress impacts immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy by examining neuroendocrine-immune pathways. It reviews mechanistic evidence linking chronic stress to T-cell exhaustion and immunosuppression, noting antidepressants' preclinical potential to improve ICI responses. The findings highlight stress as a host factor affecting ICI outcomes and emphasize the need for mechanistic interventions targeting stress pathways.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Chronic stress activates the HPA axis and sympathetic nervous system, promoting CD8+ T-cell exhaustion and regulatory T-cell expansion",
    "Antidepressants show preclinical potential to remodel the tumor immune microenvironment and enhance T-cell function",
    "Emotional stress may influence ICI efficacy through neuroendocrine-immune networks, requiring further mechanistic investigation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies emotional stress as a modifiable host factor that can influence immune checkpoint inhibitor responses via neuroendocrine-immune mechanisms, providing a foundation for targeted therapeutic strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how plants detect 2',3'-cyclic nucleotide monophosphates (2',3'-cNMPs) produced by insect saliva. Researchers identified NIB1, a rice glycine-rich RNA-binding protein, that binds 2',3'-cAMP, 2',3'-cGMP, and ApG>p from insect RNases. Binding triggers nuclear condensates that recruit EDS1, activating plant immunity. The findings reveal a conserved mechanism where plant RNA-binding proteins sense nuclease-generated signals to initiate defense responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "NIB1 senses 2',3'-cAMP, 2',3'-cGMP, and ApG>p produced by insect salivary RNases",
    "NIB1 binding forms nuclear condensates recruiting EDS1 to activate immune responses",
    "This pathway links plant TIR nuclease activity to EDS1-mediated immunity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery establishes a conserved plant immune mechanism where RNA-binding proteins detect nuclease-generated second messengers to initiate defense signaling, bridging insect effector activity and innate immunity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether TIR domains in animal innate immune receptors, specifically TLR4, exhibit catalytic activity beyond scaffolding. Using biochemical assays, researchers discovered TLR4 TIR domain's NADase activity produces adenosine diphosphate ribose, which remains trapped to stabilize a catalytic pocket with TIRAP, enabling signalosome assembly. This 'produce-and-trap' mechanism links enzymatic function to immune signaling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TLR4 TIR domain exhibits NADase activity with single-turnover kinetics",
    "Adenosine d. ribose is entrapped rather than released, acting as molecular glue",
    "The trapped product stabilizes TIRAP to nucleate innate immune signalosome assembly"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work reveals a novel enzymatic mechanism in innate immunity where catalytic product retention drives signalosome assembly, integrating enzymatic activity with immune signaling pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates dual sympathetic and parasympathetic nerve modulation to combat postoperative prostate cancer progression. Using personalized nanotechnology-enabled therapy (ADNT), the researchers codelivered a β-blocker and muscarinic receptor antagonist via hybrid nanovesicles in murine models. ADNT delayed recurrence and metastasis, reduced autonomic nerve infiltration, remodeled neuro-immune crosstalk and chemokine networks, and alleviated cachexia and anxiety. Combined with immune checkpoint blockade, it achieved complete responses in all treated mice, demonstrating clinical translatability in human specimens.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ADNT delays postoperative recurrence and metastasis in highly invasive murine prostate cancer models",
    "ADNT reduces autonomic nerve infiltration and remodels neuro-immune crosstalk and chemokine networks",
    "ADNT combined with immune checkpoint blockade induces complete tumor regression in 100% of mice"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach establishes dual neuromodulation as a viable strategy to disrupt cancer progression by targeting neuro-immune interactions and chemokine signaling, offering a novel therapeutic avenue for prostate cancer."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed an eight-gene prognostic model using platelet-related genes (PRGs) to predict survival in gastric cancer (GC) patients. RNA-seq data from TCGA and GEO identified 123 PRGs, with the model validated via RT-qPCR. The model showed distinct immune infiltration patterns between risk groups, including M2 macrophages and T-cell subsets, and implicated regulatory axes in GC progression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "An eight-gene model (THPO, MMRN1, EGF, SPARC, GNAI1, CD36, SERPINE1, ADAMTS18) predicts gastric cancer survival",
    "Prognostic PRGs correlate with immune cell populations, including M2 macrophages and activated memory CD4+ T cells",
    "Single-cell analysis revealed prognostic genes are expressed in epithelial cells and fibroblasts, with two regulatory axes implicated in GC progression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This model provides a mechanistic link between platelet-related gene expression and gastric cancer immune microenvironment, advancing prognostic stratification beyond clinical factors."
}

{
  "summary": "This study assesses how severe drought, compounded by warming, affects extinction risk in cacti using species distribution models. By integrating drought data with 648,316 cactus records, it found that including severe drought increased species losing suitable habitat from 58-61% to 69-72% across climate scenarios. The results highlight the critical role of climatic extremes in biodiversity vulnerability assessments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Including severe drought in models improved predictive accuracy for 91% of cactus species compared to mean-climate models",
    "Severe drought increased the proportion of cacti losing suitable habitat by 11-15% across emissions scenarios",
    "Reducing dispersal to 0 km raised habitat loss for 84-85% of species under severe drought conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that climatic extremes significantly alter biodiversity vulnerability projections under climate change, emphasizing the necessity of incorporating extreme events in conservation planning."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates an AI-monitored bioadhesive system for sutureless microvascular anastomosis. The approach integrates a hydrophobic polymeric matrix with tetrahedral microneedles to create robust vascular bonding, coupled with AI-assisted wireless sensors for real-time hemodynamic monitoring. In rat models, the system reduced procedural time by 78% and suppressed neointimal hyperplasia, demonstrating enhanced anastomosis stability and early complication detection.",
  "key_findings": [
    "iMAS reduced procedural time by 78% in rat models",
    "iMAS suppressed neointimal hyperplasia",
    "AI-assisted sensors enabled real-time monitoring of vascular hemodynamics and graft health"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This platform provides a novel method for rapid, secure microvascular anastomosis with integrated real-time monitoring, advancing techniques for vascular surgery and transplantation."
}

{
  "summary": "This review synthesizes advances in organic electrochemical transistors (OECTs) by unifying molecular design, device architecture, and application strategies. It identifies the electrolyte-channel interface as critical for bioelectronic integration, analyzing p-type, n-type, and biodegradable conductors across diverse electrolytes and device forms. The study highlights OECT-native platforms enabling closed-loop sensing, computation, and actuation while addressing biocompatibility and standardization for next-generation bioelectronic interfaces.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The electrolyte-channel region is pivotal for convergence of biology and electronics in OECTs",
    "OECTs support closed-loop systems integrating sensing, memory, computation, and actuation",
    "Biodegradable and stable conductors enable diverse applications from implantable devices to plant-bioelectronic systems"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a unified framework for designing bioelectronic interfaces that bridge biological and electronic functions through OECTs, advancing the field toward autonomous, multi-functional systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the role of PI3Kδ in regulatory T-cell differentiation within the thymus. Using a spontaneously arising NOD mouse model with a Pik3cd nonsense mutation, the researchers demonstrated reduced differentiation of PD-1-expressing Tregs. In vitro and in vivo inhibition of PI3Kδ and downstream PDK-1/AKT/mTOR signaling significantly impaired PD-1+ Treg development. Transcriptomic analysis revealed PI3Kδ signaling modulates gene expression for both Treg suppressive functions and CTLA-4, indicating its central role in thymic Treg maturation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A NOD mouse model with a Pik3cd nonsense mutation showed reduced differentiation of PD-1-expressing regulatory T cells in the thymus",
    "Pharmacological inhibition of PI3Kδ and downstream PDK-1/AKT/mTOR signaling impaired PD-1+ Treg differentiation",
    "PI3Kδ signaling modulates expression of genes critical for Treg suppressive functions and CTLA-4"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PI3Kδ as a pivotal regulator of regulatory T-cell differentiation in the thymus, providing mechanistic insights into how PI3Kδ signaling balances Treg functional potential through gene expression modulation."
}
